2E FORTH OS MEMORY MAP

0200-02FF  TERMINAL INPUT BUFFER
0400-07FF  TEXT SCREEN, BOTH BANKS
0800-08FF  ONE RAW DISK SECTOR
0900-09FF  VTOC WORKING COPY
0A00-0AFF  TRACK/SECTOR LIST
0D00-0DFF  BOOT SOURCE SECTOR
0F00-0FFF  PAD
1000-1FFF  PARSED CATALOG
2000-3FFF  HI-RES PAGE 1, BOTH BANKS
4000-80FF  KERNEL
8100-BFFF  THE USER'S DICTIONARY
D000-F5FF  THE SYSTEM'S OWN DICTIONARY,
           IN THE LANGUAGE CARD
FFFA-FFFF  CPU VECTORS, COPIED FROM ROM

ZERO PAGE 0000-004F IS THE MONITOR'S.
0050-009F IS THE FORTH DATA STACK.  THE
RETURN STACK IS THE 6502'S OWN, ON PAGE
ONE.

THERE IS NO DOS.  9600-BFFF USED TO BE
DOS 3.3 AND IS DICTIONARY NOW.
